{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1157","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Inverse of Rows and Columns"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a binary matrix $$$a$$$ of size $$$n \\times m$$$. A binary matrix is a matrix where each element is either $$$0$$$ or $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may perform some (possibly zero) operations with this matrix. During each operation you can inverse the row of this matrix or a column of this matrix. Formally, inverting a row is changing all values in this row to the opposite ($$$0$$$ to $$$1$$$, $$$1$$$ to $$$0$$$). Inverting a column is changing all values in this column to the opposite."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to sort the initial matrix by some sequence of such operations. The matrix is considered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sorted"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the array $$$[a_{1, 1}, a_{1, 2}, \\dots, a_{1, m}, a_{2, 1}, a_{2, 2}, \\dots, a_{2, m}, \\dots, a_{n, m - 1}, a_{n, m}]$$$ is sorted "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in non-descending order"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 200$$$) — the number of rows and the number of columns in the matrix."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$n$$$ lines contain $$$m$$$ integers each. The $$$j$$$-th element in the $$$i$$$-th line is $$$a_{i, j}$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_{i, j} \\le 1$$$) — the element of $$$a$$$ at position $$$(i, j)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible to obtain a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sorted"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" matrix, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in the first line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in the first line. In the second line print a string $$$r$$$ of length $$$n$$$. The $$$i$$$-th character $$$r_i$$$ of this string should be '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' if the $$$i$$$-th row of the matrix is inverted and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' otherwise. In the third line print a string $$$c$$$ of length $$$m$$$. The $$$j$$$-th character $$$c_j$$$ of this string should be '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' if the $$$j$$$-th column of the matrix is inverted and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' otherwise. If there are multiple answers, you can print any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},